WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.768
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:03.203
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:05.672
between M&amp;M's in the UK and the US.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:06.773
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:11.077
Here in the US, we have eight

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:13.613
different portion sizes of M&amp;M's.

00:00:13.613 --> 00:00:14.514
All the way at the end here,

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:17.083
the smallest portion is
known as the fun size.

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:20.520
This little guy is 0.6
ounces, or 18 grams.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.690
Then, single size bag, 1.69 ounces.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.258
Then we go up to the box.

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:28.294
This is 3.1 ounces, or 87 grams.

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:29.662
Now we have the share size.

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:30.997
Peanut makes its first appearance.

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:34.667
This is 3.27 ounces, or 92.7 grams.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:35.635
Little bigger of a pouch,

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:38.738
we have the 10.7-ounce, or 303-gram,

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:40.740
sharing-size pouch part two.

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.342
Then we jump up to the family size.

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:45.612
This is 19.2 ounces, 545 grams.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:47.747
Throwing a party? M&amp;M's got you covered.

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:48.915
This is the party pack.

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:51.885
38 ounces, 1,105 grams.

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:55.155
And the biggest portion
size you can get is this,

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:57.390
the pantry-size tub.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:02.028
62 ounces, 1,757 grams.

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:04.931
In the UK, M&amp;M's come in
four standard portion sizes.

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:06.666
Around the holidays, you
can get a selection box

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:09.269
with a small packet of
M&amp;M's that weighs 45 grams,

00:01:09.269 --> 00:01:10.870
but unfortunately, we
couldn't get one today.

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.273
Our standard pouch is 125 grams.

00:01:13.273 --> 00:01:15.041
Then we move up to a more-to-share bag,

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:18.111
which, for standard chocolate
M&amp;M's, comes with 250 grams.

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:20.580
The largest size available
in the UK is a party bag.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.115
I went to about eight
different supermarkets

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:23.116
and I couldn't find one,

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:25.452
but usually they would
contain 1 kilogram of M&amp;M's,

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:26.519
so we're going to make our own.

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:35.795
There is our unofficial party-size bag.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:37.230
1 kilogram of M&amp;M's.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.865
All said, America's largest size

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:42.435
is 75.7% larger than the UK's.

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.537
In the UK, the portion
sizes also vary slightly

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:46.673
depending on which flavor
of M&amp;M's you've opted for.

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:49.709
A more-to-share bag of
chocolate M&amp;M's is 250 grams,

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:53.413
but a more-to-share bag of
crispy M&amp;M's is just 246 grams.

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:55.014
If you want the most value in the UK,

00:01:55.014 --> 00:01:56.082
opt for peanut M&amp;M's.

00:01:56.082 --> 00:01:59.319
A more-to-share bag of
those contains 268 grams.

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:00.987
Are the M&amp;M's themselves different sizes

00:02:00.987 --> 00:02:01.921
in the UK and the US?

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:03.857
We're going to weigh out
100 grams of chocolate M&amp;M's

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:05.258
and count them to see how many you get.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:07.327
One, two, three ...

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:09.562
Two, three, four, five ...

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:12.499
[fast-forwarding]

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:14.267
That is so annoying!

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:16.402
It was so close to being 100 grams

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:17.570
of exactly 100 M&amp;M's,

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:19.906
but instead 100 grams
of UK chocolate M&amp;M's

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.875
is 102 M&amp;M's.

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:25.044
100 grams of American M&amp;M's

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:28.414
is 114 M&amp;M's.

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.049
So what does that mean, ours are smaller?

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:31.551
And how do we feel about that?

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.153
I don't know if it's better or worse.

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:35.054
But portion size don't stop there.

00:02:35.054 --> 00:02:37.891
You can also buy M&amp;M's
directly from the M&amp;M website.

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:39.058
The main purpose of this seems to be

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:41.561
catering for large events
like weddings or parties.

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:43.863
You can technically get
smaller-than-average portion sizes,

00:02:43.863 --> 00:02:45.331
but only in bulk quantities.

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:47.734
For example, in the US, you can get these.

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:50.170
Tiny party-favor packs of M&amp;M's

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:53.473
weighing just 0.75 ounces each.

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:55.742
Or they have party-favor tins,

00:02:55.742 --> 00:02:58.912
which contain 1.5 ounces of M&amp;M's.

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:00.613
But both of these have to have a minimum

00:03:00.613 --> 00:03:02.949
of 20 or more units.

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:05.351
Now, what doesn't require a minimum order,

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.753
however, are the bulk bags.

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:08.521
In the US you can order bulk bags

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:11.925
of 1 pound, 2 pounds, or 5 pounds.

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:14.427
Now, technically, you could
order 10 pounds of M&amp;M's,

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:16.596
but they just send you two 5-pound bags,

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:18.932
which is a bit disappointing,
so we just got one.

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:20.600
5-pounder.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:21.701
Look at these M&amp;M's.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.570
The UK website is a similar situation.

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:26.906
Our smallest portion size is
this 28-gram designer case.

00:03:26.906 --> 00:03:28.875
But the minimum order for these is 20.

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:31.144
Unlike the US, we only
have one bulk-bag order.

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:33.446
And that's this one,
which is 1.5 kilograms.

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:36.616
That's around 3.3 pounds,
which is a 34% decrease

00:03:36.616 --> 00:03:38.851
from the largest single
bag size in the US.

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.153
If you do order M&amp;M's on the website,

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:41.221
you can customize them.

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.655
We chose some custom colors

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:44.824
and also put some custom
text on the M&amp;M's.

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:45.959
In terms of colors, I went for this

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:47.193
lovely blue-and-white color scheme

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:49.462
to match my stunning M&amp;M's T-shirt.

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.465
Then I had some fun putting
some text options on there.

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:54.767
Firstly, I went for "Harry &lt;3 Joe."

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:55.935
We also had to rep the show,

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:57.570
so I put a "Food Wars" one on there.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:58.972
Then, because I have the mind of a child,

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:00.773
I tried to put some
swear words on the M&amp;M's,

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:02.675
and it turns out they
actually try and censor you.

00:04:02.675 --> 00:04:04.944
For example, if you try and
put the word "poop" on an M&amp;M,

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:06.145
a warning message will flash up

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:07.714
telling you to get in touch with the team.

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:08.982
But there is a work-around.

00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:10.183
For example, for the word "poop,"

00:04:10.183 --> 00:04:12.085
by replacing the O's with 0s,

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:13.419
I was able to get around the censorship

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:14.754
and create poop M&amp;M's.

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:17.924
The same goes for replacing
the I with a 1 in "penis"

00:04:17.924 --> 00:04:20.426
and replacing the A with a 4 in "balls."

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:23.463
This is some serious journalism
taking place right here.

00:04:23.463 --> 00:04:26.699
Now, Harry, of course,
went with customizing M&amp;M's

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:28.635
with fun words and stuff on it.

00:04:28.635 --> 00:04:30.703
I just went for pictures.

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:33.473
You can get custom images on an M&amp;M.

00:04:33.473 --> 00:04:35.575
So what I did is I got

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:39.379
Harry face and Joe face M&amp;M's.

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:40.513
OK, that'll show 'em.

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:45.685
Here are all the ingredients
in chocolate M&amp;M's in the UK.

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:49.922
And here is everything in a bag

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:52.925
of classic M&amp;M's in the US.

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:54.394
Look at all those colors.

00:04:54.394 --> 00:04:55.428
A few things to note here.

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:56.929
Firstly, the food colorings used

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:58.698
in the two countries are wildly different.

00:04:58.698 --> 00:05:00.500
In the UK, some of our colors are natural,

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.835
including the curcumin and the carotenes.

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:06.005
Whereas in the US, all
our colors are artificial.

00:05:06.005 --> 00:05:08.341
Blue No. 1 is used in
both the US and the UK,

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:11.210
but we also have Blue No. 2, Red 40,

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:13.313
Yellow 5, and Yellow 6.

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:15.515
Blue 2 is a less common one.

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:17.950
It's also known as indigo carmine.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:20.320
Now, the good news is it won't
make your kids hyperactive.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:23.089
The more interesting news is that Blue 2

00:05:23.089 --> 00:05:25.325
is filtered rapidly through the kidneys,

00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:29.996
and consuming enough of it
will turn your pee blue.

00:05:29.996 --> 00:05:31.864
The practical use of this is so doctors

00:05:31.864 --> 00:05:34.934
can highlight your urinary
tract for surgeries.

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:37.837
A less practical effect or use
is to freak out your friends.

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:39.872
Hey-o, we're doing jokes
in the script, apparently.

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:41.774
Hey, welcome to "Food Wars"!

00:05:41.774 --> 00:05:44.043
So anyway, turns your piss blue.

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:45.044
Speaking of carmine,

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:47.113
what about the carmine
used in British M&amp;M's?

00:05:47.113 --> 00:05:48.948
Standard carmine is a red food coloring

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:51.217
with the code names Red 4 or E120.

00:05:51.217 --> 00:05:52.285
It's a natural food dye,

00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:54.220
but what is the natural source, you ask?

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.555
It's cochineal beetles.

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:58.257
If you grind up cochineal beetles,

00:05:58.257 --> 00:05:59.292
you're left with a red powder,

00:05:59.292 --> 00:06:01.060
which when mixed with
water and some chemicals

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.762
can be turned into a very stable dye.

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:04.764
Obviously, we're going to now
have to try and make our own.

00:06:11.337 --> 00:06:13.740
But you can see the red color
coming off of it already.

00:06:15.541 --> 00:06:17.210
Now I'm going to try and
put some of this in there,

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.746
mix it with some water,
and see what happens.

00:06:21.481 --> 00:06:23.916
That has really worked. Wow.

00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:25.952
Look how red that is! That's incredible.

00:06:25.952 --> 00:06:27.420
As you can see, just by
chopping up some beetles

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:29.455
and mixing it with water,
we've got this incredible

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:31.424
kind of blood-red food dye.

00:06:31.424 --> 00:06:32.959
Now, while apparently
synthetic alternatives

00:06:32.959 --> 00:06:34.961
to carmine do exist, M&amp;M's confirmed to us

00:06:34.961 --> 00:06:37.196
that the carmine they use does
in fact come from beetles.

00:06:37.196 --> 00:06:40.066
So, technically, every time
you eat a red M&amp;M in the UK,

00:06:40.066 --> 00:06:41.300
you're eating bugs.

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:44.170
So, do you want your kids hyperactive,

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.272
or do you want them eating beetles?

00:06:46.272 --> 00:06:47.507
Not much of a choice, is it?

