00:10:06.038 --> 00:10:07.406
but use the M&amp;M's branding.

00:10:07.406 --> 00:10:09.408
The main event here is probably this.

00:10:09.408 --> 00:10:12.778
This is an M&amp;M's chocolate
ball-pool party cake.

00:10:12.778 --> 00:10:14.213
It says it serves 26.

00:10:14.213 --> 00:10:15.247
I'm really struggling to see

00:10:15.247 --> 00:10:17.016
how you'd even cut that into 26 pieces,

00:10:17.016 --> 00:10:19.885
let alone have slices which
would then satisfy people.

00:10:19.885 --> 00:10:21.354
He's smiling, but he
looks like he's kind of

00:10:21.354 --> 00:10:22.989
smiling through the pain at the moment.

00:10:22.989 --> 00:10:24.190
I feel you, buddy.

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:27.360
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:29.629
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

00:10:29.629 --> 00:10:30.663
Oh, God.

00:10:31.931 --> 00:10:33.766
[laughs]

00:10:33.766 --> 00:10:34.667
There we go.

00:10:34.667 --> 00:10:36.202
Can you eat him, or is he plastic?

00:10:36.202 --> 00:10:37.036
Let's find out.

00:10:38.037 --> 00:10:39.271
I would assume edible.

00:10:41.507 --> 00:10:43.309
He's edible. I'm not
sure what he's made of.

00:10:43.309 --> 00:10:44.343
He does not taste good.

00:10:44.343 --> 00:10:46.178
OK, I'm cutting myself a little piece.

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:51.917
It's actually really not terrible.

00:10:51.917 --> 00:10:53.085
If I were 8 years old again

00:10:53.085 --> 00:10:55.254
and someone gave me a piece
of this at a birthday party,

00:10:55.254 --> 00:10:56.155
I wouldn't complain.

00:10:56.155 --> 00:10:57.056
Following on from the cake,

00:10:57.056 --> 00:10:58.991
we've got a few more exclusive
M&amp;M's products in the UK,

00:10:58.991 --> 00:11:00.660
starting with these chocolate bars.

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:02.094
You guys can get these in the US as well.

00:11:02.094 --> 00:11:04.597
I think we share the peanut
and the milk chocolate options,

00:11:04.597 --> 00:11:06.666
but we have crispy as an exclusive

00:11:06.666 --> 00:11:08.167
and cookie as an exclusive.

00:11:08.167 --> 00:11:09.468
They're basically just milk chocolate bars

00:11:09.468 --> 00:11:12.338
with little pieces of crispy
M&amp;M's or cookies inside.

00:11:12.338 --> 00:11:14.874
Correct, we do have the chocolate bars

00:11:14.874 --> 00:11:15.975
here in the US as well.

00:11:15.975 --> 00:11:18.177
But one exclusive we have is this,

00:11:18.177 --> 00:11:21.580
the almond M&amp;M's chocolate bar.

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:24.083
Next up we have this M&amp;M's
spread with crispy pieces.

00:11:24.083 --> 00:11:26.118
Now, it's a chocolate- and
hazelnut-flavored spread

00:11:26.118 --> 00:11:27.453
with crispy M&amp;M's inside.

00:11:27.453 --> 00:11:30.156
So it's basically like a
Nutella and M&amp;M hybrid.

00:11:32.925 --> 00:11:34.427
Well, yeah, I'm actually
pretty impressed by this.

00:11:34.427 --> 00:11:36.028
It tastes basically the same as Nutella.

00:11:36.028 --> 00:11:37.229
I don't know if they're actual M&amp;M's

00:11:37.229 --> 00:11:39.231
or just kind of the crispy
rice pieces inside this,

00:11:39.231 --> 00:11:41.100
but either way, adds a nice little crunch,

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:42.201
you know, a bit of texture.

00:11:42.201 --> 00:11:44.370
Next up, we have these M&amp;M's
double chocolate cookies.

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:45.705
Now, the double chocolate in the name

00:11:45.705 --> 00:11:47.406
comes from the fact that
they are chocolate cookies

00:11:47.406 --> 00:11:49.341
and then they also
contain chocolate M&amp;M's.

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:54.814
You know, as far as a crunchy
UK cookie goes, not too bad.

00:11:54.814 --> 00:11:56.916
Next up, we've got two Easter egg options.

00:11:56.916 --> 00:11:58.718
It's a sort of hollow chocolate egg,

00:11:58.718 --> 00:12:00.853
usually comes with a
couple of bags of sweets

00:12:00.853 --> 00:12:02.688
of your choosing, in this case, M&amp;M's.

00:12:02.688 --> 00:12:04.156
They're given to kids around Easter time

00:12:04.156 --> 00:12:05.157
to celebrate the holiday.

00:12:05.157 --> 00:12:06.525
Now, for M&amp;M's, these are available

00:12:06.525 --> 00:12:08.527
as either brownie or crispy options.

00:12:08.527 --> 00:12:10.129
I actually don't know if
Americans do Easter eggs.

00:12:10.129 --> 00:12:11.464
Joe, is that a thing in the States?

00:12:11.464 --> 00:12:14.433
Easter eggs, Easter
candy, Easter chocolate,

00:12:14.433 --> 00:12:16.669
Easter baskets, Easter bunny,

00:12:16.669 --> 00:12:19.538
all that stuff is very
popular in America as well.

00:12:19.538 --> 00:12:21.140
We can also get a bunch of nonstandard

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:22.441
M&amp;M's stuff here in the US.

00:12:22.441 --> 00:12:26.545
For instance, we have M&amp;M
cookie ice cream sandwiches.

00:12:26.545 --> 00:12:28.714
Weird, these boxes are
open. That's so weird.

00:12:28.714 --> 00:12:30.116
It says four, but
there's only two in here.

00:12:30.116 --> 00:12:31.117
I don't know what happened.

00:12:31.117 --> 00:12:35.054
You can get them in
mint, classic chocolate,

00:12:35.054 --> 00:12:37.423
and vanilla.

00:12:37.423 --> 00:12:39.225
There's also a chocolate one

00:12:39.225 --> 00:12:40.860
with ice cream that's also chocolate.

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.762
That is not available in my area.

00:12:42.762 --> 00:12:45.131
See that? And then they got
the ice cream right there.

00:12:45.131 --> 00:12:46.432
We also have something called

00:12:46.432 --> 00:12:50.369
the Valentine's Day M&amp;M popcorn bucket.

00:12:50.369 --> 00:12:54.473
One, two, three packets of popcorn,

00:12:54.473 --> 00:12:55.875
two boxes,

00:12:55.875 --> 00:12:58.544
one of the milk chocolate
and one of the peanut.

00:12:58.544 --> 00:13:01.847
Also something that I got similar to this,

00:13:01.847 --> 00:13:03.282
and I think it's an exclusive,

00:13:03.282 --> 00:13:08.287
it is milk chocolate
popcorn-flavored M&amp;M's.

00:13:09.789 --> 00:13:13.058
It's weird. Tastes like
popcorn and chocolate.

00:13:13.058 --> 00:13:14.393
Now, in preparation for this episode,

00:13:14.393 --> 00:13:16.095
I did something which no true Londoner

00:13:16.095 --> 00:13:17.029
should ever have to do,

00:13:17.029 --> 00:13:19.265
which is visit M&amp;M's
World in Leicester Square.

00:13:19.265 --> 00:13:20.432
Now, according to signs in the shop,

00:13:20.432 --> 00:13:22.067
it's the largest candy shop in Europe

00:13:22.067 --> 00:13:24.136
and also has the world's
largest candy wall.

00:13:24.136 --> 00:13:26.238
I'm gonna be honest, I
absolutely hate M&amp;M's World

00:13:26.238 --> 00:13:27.606
and pretty much everything it stands for.

00:13:27.606 --> 00:13:30.409
It's kind of like walking
into the museum of capitalism.

00:13:30.409 --> 00:13:32.077
It's somehow an even bigger tourist trap

00:13:32.077 --> 00:13:33.245
than, like, Buckingham Palace.

00:13:33.245 --> 00:13:35.181
I just don't understand why
people would come to London

00:13:35.181 --> 00:13:36.949
and make a beeline for the M&amp;M's store.

00:13:36.949 --> 00:13:38.851
So, I've not been to the
M&amp;M's store in London,

00:13:38.851 --> 00:13:40.319
but I've definitely been to the one

00:13:40.319 --> 00:13:42.354
in New York City, in Times Square.

00:13:42.354 --> 00:13:45.558
And I mean this as sincerely as possible,

00:13:45.558 --> 00:13:47.226
it's awesome.

00:13:47.226 --> 00:13:48.060
I'd never been in before,

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:49.428
and I wasn't really sure what to expect.

00:13:49.428 --> 00:13:50.596
And I was disappointed, honestly.

00:13:50.596 --> 00:13:51.597
I was expecting at least

00:13:51.597 --> 00:13:53.599
some kind of innovative M&amp;M flavors,

00:13:53.599 --> 00:13:54.533
but it was just the same flavors

00:13:54.533 --> 00:13:55.801
that you can normally buy in the store.

00:13:55.801 --> 00:13:58.137
It's just kind of different
colors and different packaging.

00:13:58.137 --> 00:13:59.538
The bulk of what they
had on offer in the store

00:13:59.538 --> 00:14:01.106
is actually M&amp;M's merch,

00:14:01.106 --> 00:14:03.843
like the grotesque shirt
that I'm wearing now,

00:14:03.843 --> 00:14:05.611
ironically, for the record.

00:14:05.611 --> 00:14:07.046
I'm just so confused as to who would spend

00:14:07.046 --> 00:14:08.113
their own money on this sort of stuff.

00:14:08.113 --> 00:14:09.949
Like, why are you loving M&amp;M's so much

00:14:09.949 --> 00:14:11.550
that you're going to pay a brand

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:14.220
to let you advertise for them?

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:16.689
Harry, you are.

00:14:16.689 --> 00:14:18.424
You know what isn't ironic?

00:14:18.424 --> 00:14:20.860
How much they made on that shirt sale.

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:22.561
This is what we do. We like things.

00:14:22.561 --> 00:14:25.497
We wear it to show people,
look at the thing I like.

00:14:25.497 --> 00:14:26.732
It's a capitalistic world

00:14:26.732 --> 00:14:29.101
and I'm a cog in the machine, fine.

00:14:29.101 --> 00:14:30.936
I can't escape, so I might
as well be comfortable.

00:14:30.936 --> 00:14:33.772
And that is my input on the matrix.

00:14:33.772 --> 00:14:36.041
Don't unplug me, I'm happy!

00:14:36.041 --> 00:14:38.210
All that said, I did find
one or two M&amp;M's products

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:39.712
which I couldn't find anywhere else.

00:14:39.712 --> 00:14:41.647
Firstly, there was one
of the M&amp;M chocolate bars

00:14:41.647 --> 00:14:43.182
with a flavor I couldn't
see anywhere else,

00:14:43.182 --> 00:14:44.416
and that's hazelnut.

00:14:44.416 --> 00:14:46.185
Then there were these
two sachets of powder.

00:14:46.185 --> 00:14:48.087
Firstly, there is a cookie mix.

00:14:48.087 --> 00:14:50.456
Apparently you add some
butter and some water to this,

00:14:50.456 --> 00:14:52.324
and then you have some
ready-to-bake M&amp;M cookies.

00:14:52.324 --> 00:14:55.561
And then, finally, we have an
M&amp;M's hot chocolate powder.

00:14:55.561 --> 00:14:56.395
You know what this means:

00:14:56.395 --> 00:14:58.097
We have to summon the mug.

00:14:58.097 --> 00:15:00.199
It's the return of Buchi
and Wumi. Cheers, guys.

00:15:00.199 --> 00:15:02.001
Oh, it's got M&amp;M's in it. Whoa.

00:15:06.705 --> 00:15:08.340
No, that's fine. It's
better than the Oreo one.

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:10.009
The bar was admittedly really low,

00:15:10.009 --> 00:15:11.477
but given the option, I would, of course,

00:15:11.477 --> 00:15:12.978
make this with milk instead of hot water,

00:15:12.978 --> 00:15:14.046
and I think if you did that,

00:15:14.046 --> 00:15:15.114
it would actually be pretty good.

00:15:15.114 --> 00:15:16.315
Carrying on from the earlier discussion

00:15:16.315 --> 00:15:17.316
about the M&amp;M's stores,

00:15:17.316 --> 00:15:18.784
I do just want to quickly call out M&amp;M's

00:15:18.784 --> 00:15:20.519
for having some really
questionable branding.

00:15:20.519 --> 00:15:22.054
A big recurring theme is that the M&amp;M's

00:15:22.054 --> 00:15:24.690
are really sexualized in all
of the marketing materials.

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:26.225
There was that TV ad where the M&amp;M

00:15:26.225 --> 00:15:27.927
was kind of in bed with that guy's wife.

00:15:27.927 --> 00:15:30.229
I feel like the green M&amp;M
gets sexualized quite a lot.

00:15:30.229 --> 00:15:32.131
And also, if you go on the
official M&amp;M's website,

00:15:32.131 --> 00:15:33.999
they have some really questionable bios.

00:15:33.999 --> 00:15:36.769
For example, if you go on
the bio of the brown M&amp;M,

00:15:36.769 --> 00:15:39.838
you'll see that she has a
turn-on listed, which is power.

00:15:39.838 --> 00:15:42.808
Her appearance is described
as "sexy, sophisticated,"

00:15:42.808 --> 00:15:45.611
and her best attribute is
her "big, beautiful brain."

00:15:45.611 --> 00:15:47.746
As part of my M&amp;M's World
visit, I did a scan,

00:15:47.746 --> 00:15:49.715
which told me which M&amp;M
I was, and I got yellow.

00:15:49.715 --> 00:15:51.083
So let's take a look at his bio.

00:15:51.083 --> 00:15:54.687
So, apparently my likes are
pretty ladies and fluffy things.

00:15:54.687 --> 00:15:57.122
My appearance is plump,
yellow, and all smiles,

00:15:57.122 --> 00:15:58.757
which, yeah, kind of accurate.

00:15:58.757 --> 00:16:00.626
Although the bad news
is I might be an incel,

00:16:00.626 --> 00:16:03.762
because my shortcomings are
that nice guys finish last.

00:16:03.762 --> 00:16:05.864
The idea of giving
these guys personalities

00:16:05.864 --> 00:16:07.499
to begin with is like, Jesus Christ,

00:16:07.499 --> 00:16:09.501
can't I just eat my candy in peace?

00:16:09.501 --> 00:16:12.104
[rewinding]

00:16:13.238 --> 00:16:14.606
In an unbelievable turn of events,

00:16:14.606 --> 00:16:17.042
the very day after we
filmed most of this episode,

00:16:17.042 --> 00:16:19.178
M&amp;M's announced that they
would be rebranding their M&amp;M's

00:16:19.178 --> 00:16:21.146
to be more representative of the consumer.

00:16:21.146 --> 00:16:22.081
They've backtracked on a lot

00:16:22.081 --> 00:16:23.582
of the sexualization of the M&amp;M's.

00:16:23.582 --> 00:16:25.517
For example, the green M&amp;M has swapped out

00:16:25.517 --> 00:16:27.019
her high heels for sneakers,

00:16:27.019 --> 00:16:28.954
and the brown M&amp;M has had the turn-ons

00:16:28.954 --> 00:16:30.489
removed from her bio on the website.

00:16:30.489 --> 00:16:31.390
This whole thing prompted

00:16:31.390 --> 00:16:33.459
an explosion of memes on the internet.

00:16:33.459 --> 00:16:35.160
Someone went to journalism school

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:37.963
to write some of these headlines,
and I respect them for it.

00:16:37.963 --> 00:16:38.797
I don't know why anyone ...

00:16:38.797 --> 00:16:41.800
if you had an opinion on
this, for or against it,

00:16:41.800 --> 00:16:43.969
you have entirely too
much time on your hands.

00:16:43.969 --> 00:16:45.704
It's also worth pointing
out that someone suggested

00:16:45.704 --> 00:16:48.040
the M&amp;M's rebrand could
be suspiciously timed

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:49.641
and that they might be
trying to draw attention

00:16:49.641 --> 00:16:51.610
away from an ongoing class action lawsuit.

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:53.045
Mars, the owner of M&amp;M's,

00:16:53.045 --> 00:16:54.847
along with several other
major chocolate producers

00:16:54.847 --> 00:16:56.915
including Hershey's, Nestlé, and more,

00:16:56.915 --> 00:16:58.384
have been accused of using cocoa

00:16:58.384 --> 00:17:01.086
from plantations which
use child slave laborers.

00:17:01.086 --> 00:17:03.155
Oh, God.

00:17:03.155 --> 00:17:04.923
Mars told Bloomberg, "We do not comment

00:17:04.923 --> 00:17:06.825
on any possible pending litigation."

00:17:06.825 --> 00:17:07.893
Oh, that's ...

00:17:07.893 --> 00:17:09.194
the fact that it wasn't a blanket,

00:17:09.194 --> 00:17:10.963
"Of course not, what?"

00:17:10.963 --> 00:17:12.264
The fact that they're like,
"Oh, we can't comment on it,"

00:17:12.264 --> 00:17:13.599
it's like, that's a yes.

00:17:13.599 --> 00:17:14.700
The lawsuit is still ongoing,

00:17:14.700 --> 00:17:17.036
so we'll have to wait and see
if any more details emerge.

00:17:17.036 --> 00:17:19.471
Was the timing of the rebrand
coincidental or cynical?

00:17:19.471 --> 00:17:20.806
We'll let you guys decide.

00:17:20.806 --> 00:17:22.107
I like how I just found out about that

00:17:22.107 --> 00:17:23.709
after I ate all these M&amp;M's.

00:17:23.709 --> 00:17:24.743
Well, if it will make
everyone feel better,

00:17:24.743 --> 00:17:27.079
I have a huge headache from
eating all this junk food.

00:17:29.481 --> 00:17:31.650
In the US, the recommended
serving size of M&amp;M's

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:34.620
is 28 grams, which is roughly 1 ounce.

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:36.055
So when it comes to classic M&amp;M's,

00:17:36.055 --> 00:17:37.723
the US version has more calories,

00:17:37.723 --> 00:17:40.526
saturated fat, carbs, and sodium.

00:17:40.526 --> 00:17:42.661
The UK M&amp;M's actually
contain more total fat

00:17:42.661 --> 00:17:43.829
as well as more sugar.

00:17:43.829 --> 00:17:45.297
Sugar is the worst nutritional offender

00:17:45.297 --> 00:17:46.698
as far as M&amp;M are concerned.

00:17:46.698 --> 00:17:49.468
28 grams of UK M&amp;M's
contains just over a third

00:17:49.468 --> 00:17:50.936
of your daily sugar allowance.

00:17:50.936 --> 00:17:52.704
What about the least
healthiest M&amp;M in the US?

00:17:52.704 --> 00:17:54.706
Well, for us, there's a two-way tie

00:17:54.706 --> 00:17:58.410
between the peanut butter and
the white chocolate peanut.

00:17:58.410 --> 00:18:01.146
Both of these contain
150 calories per 28 grams

00:18:01.146 --> 00:18:03.248
as well as 8 grams of fat.

00:18:03.248 --> 00:18:05.517
In the UK, our least
healthy M&amp;M is peanut.

00:18:05.517 --> 00:18:07.719
A 28-gram serving of UK peanut M&amp;M's

00:18:07.719 --> 00:18:09.721
will contain 144 calories

00:18:09.721 --> 00:18:13.192
as well as a slightly increased
7.28 grams of total fat.

00:18:13.192 --> 00:18:15.360
I put my body on the line for content.

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:18.564
I have no idea if that
was fact-checked or not,

00:18:18.564 --> 00:18:20.799
but like everyone else, I read
something on the internet,

00:18:20.799 --> 00:18:22.868
it sounds true, that's good enough for me.

